== Sliced Vegetables ==

Slice the vegetables: Use a #mandoline slicer{} or #chef knife{} to slice the @yellow squash{2%small}, @zucchini{2%small to medium}, @roma tomatoes{4}, and @eggplant{1%medium to large} into 1/8-inch-thick pieces.

> Tip: If the size of vegetables varies, you can cut the bigger slices in half or into quarters.

Salt the vegetables and let them sit: Prepare two large #baking pans{} with a pinch of @salt{} on the bottom of the pans. Then arrange the vegetables on the pan with another generous pinch of salt over top. Let the vegetables sit with the salt for ~{30%minutes}.

> Note: This helps tenderize the eggplant and zucchini and removes excess moisture from the vegetables, preventing the dish from getting watery. However, this step can be skipped, and the vegetables can be layered into the dish if you prefer to reduce your prep time.

== Roasted Pepper ==

Roast the red pepper: Place a #wired rack{} over a #gas range{} and roast the @red bell pepper{1} directly on the open flame of your range. Rotate every few minutes until the whole pepper is nicely charred. After, place it in a #bowl{} and cover with #foil{} for ~{10-15%minutes}. Then use #paper towels{} to remove most of the charring from the outside, remove the core, and dice the pepper.

> Note: if you don't have a gas range, you can do this with a dry cast-iron pan on the stovetop, or on a grill, or skip this step and add the bell pepper with the tomatoes to the sauce. You can also substitute with jarred roasted pepper to make it easier!

== Sauce ==

Make the sauce: In a large pan or #Dutch oven pot{}, add the @olive oil{2%tablespoons} and saute the @onion{2/3%medium}(diced), @celery stalk{1}(diced), and @carrot{1}(diced) with a pinch of @salt{} until soft (about ~{3%minutes}). Then add the @garlic cloves{4}(minced or pressed) and cook for another ~{1%minute}. Then add the @roma tomatoes{4}(diced), the diced fire-roasted bell pepper, @garlic powder{1/4%teaspoon}, @red pepper flakes{1/8%teaspoon}, @black pepper{1/4%teaspoon}, and a generous pinch of @salt{}. Let the vegetables cook for about ~{8%minutes} on a medium heat, stirring often. Then add @fresh thyme{1%teaspoon} and a splash of @dry red wine{1%splash} and let the wine cook for an additional ~{2-3%minutes}. Then add in torn @fresh basil{2%Tablespoons} leaves.

Blend the sauce ingredients: Carefully transfer the cooked sauce ingredients to a #blender{}, and blend on high for ~{30%seconds} until the consistency is creamy and smooth. Taste the sauce and adjust with additional @salt{to taste} and pepper if needed.

== Ratatouille ==

Prepare the ratatouille: Use paper towels to pat the salted vegetables dry. In a #casserole dish{} (I used a 3.5-quart #braiser{}), spread the sauce on the bottom. Then arrange the sliced squash, zucchini, tomatoes, and eggplants in a circular pattern in the dish, using up all the ingredients that you can fit.

> Note: I like to alternate between the different vegetables, but you might run out of some before the others, so you can double up on what you have the most of.

Bake: Cover the dish with a lid or tightly with foil, and bake at 375F for ~{45%minutes}. Then remove the lid/foil, sprinkle @freshly grated Parmigiano Reggiano{1/2%cup} on top of the ratatouille, and broil on high for ~{1-2%minutes}, or until the cheese is melted and browned. Let cool for several minutes before serving!